From 4f3c46415216dfdbbafd76ff2ad0471a001ff831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AKADATA LIMITED <linux@saphira.vm2.uk>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:52:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ccram: software-compressed object store + self-test (Phase
 2A, unwired)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Part of CCRAM — AKADATA LIMITED adaptation of Meta CRAM (see
CRAM.PROVENANCE in linux-saphira-meta-cram; Saphira-original code,
GPL-2.0-only).

Standalone 4096-byte page -> LZ4 object store, proven on its own
before any residency wiring: variable-sized objects with original
length, stored length, algo/flags, xxhash64 and backing handle pack
into 512-byte units over node-local chunk pages held off-LRU;
incompressible pages store raw as 8 units.  lib/lz4 and xxhash64 are
reused; zsmalloc/zswap/async-crypto were audited and deliberately not
reused (recorded in the file header).  Compression uses per-CPU
scratch only; every store allocation is NORETRY|NOWARN fail-fast with
caller fallback, so no reclaim cycle can form.  Exact-once release via
erase-then-release refcounting.

Includes a deterministic self-test (zeros/ones/patterns/counter/
textlike/random/half: store, class check, load, memcmp+hash, free,
double-free refusal, leak balance) that runs once on a throwaway
store when ccram.compress=lz4 is given, plus debugfs store_stats and
a selftest retrigger.  A failed self-test disables compression and
the tier keeps serving 1:1, fail closed.  Default off.  No existing
CCRAM or CRAM file is modified by this commit.
